From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Priestley <Voicedrew11@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:09:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] Audit and fix VIF1/VU1 emulation against hardware specs

Fixed VIF1 UNPACK:
- V2 now writes v1v0v1v0 pattern; V3/V4 components properly ordered
- V4-5 format: 5:5:5:1 components at correct bit positions
- STMOD MODE=3 (ROW=data) support added
- MPG destination masked to (imm & 0x7FF)*8, wrapping at 16 KB

Fixed VU1:
- EFU opcodes: ERSQRT=0x79, ESIN=0x7C, EATAN=0x7D, EEXP=0x7E
- EATAN coefficient precision corrected
- RSQRT(0,0) produces signed zero, not saturated max
- XGKICK address mask to (VI & 0x3FF)*16 for 16 KB wrap
- Removed dead condition wrappers in clip flag tests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
